
,Chelsea was here 10-12-21 - Hold real name, set #Name to handle/knob name from selector, then search CSV table for values appropriate...

,This is where I need to uncover HK selection and assign the appropriate name to #HKName.
Load, DoorAndDrawer-RoomToHardwareMatching.PCB

Set, #TempHKtotalUnitCost=0

Set, #HoldUnitCode=<#Code>
Set, #HoldUnitLength=<#Length>
Set, #HoldUnitWidth=<#Width>
Set, #HoldUnitDepth=<#Depth>



,Chelsea was here 5-16-23 - Initialize the following at zero, these get set on DrawerHandleKnob and DoorHandleKnob
Set, #TAGHardwareH=0
Set, #TAGHardwareK=0

,Chelsea was here 10-7-21 - We're reading TAG Hardware handle names, if one matches we get a new handle cost. This needs to go out on the counter.
  ReadCSVFile,Tag Hardware Handles and Knobs.csv,1,2,3
  ReadCsvValue,Tag Hardware Handles and Knobs.csv,#HKName,#HKCode,#TempHKtotalunitCost

Load, CountDoorAndDrawer-RoomToHardwareMatching.PCB

Do,(1=2):1,SKIP THIS FOR NOW
{
,The Do statement below is to give the TAG handle cost to the collection for the array.

Do, (#TempHKTotalUnitCost>0):1
{
Set, #Name=#HKName
Set, #Code="#HKCode"
Set, #Length="X"
Set, #Width="X"
Set, #Depth="X"
Set, #QuantityLoop=0
Set, #TotalUnitCost=[#TempHKTotalUnitCost]

Set, #TAGHardwareK=[#CURRENTKnobCount]
Set, #TAGHardwareH=[#CURRENTHandleCount]



  , IF I'm a TAG handle, then set handle cost if I'm a TAG knob set knob cost
  Set, #TagKCost=[#TempHKTotalUnitCost]
  Set, #TagHCost=[#TempHKTotalUnitCost]
  

  ,Right now total unit cost will be the single handle/knob cost for the array purposes.
   Set, #TotalUnitCost=[#TempHKTotalUnitCost]
  ,Sets loop quantity for the array
   ,Set, #LoopQuantity=[NUM*(#TAGHardwareK+#TAGHardwareH)]

  ,Starting with 1...
     ,  Set, #QuantityLoop=1

  ,Chelsea was here 11-12-21 - Clipped the "While" structure from !! KCD Frame
  ,  Loop through per handle/knob for array.

 , While, (#QuantityLoop<=#LoopQuantity)

      ,Load, CommonTAGHardwareCounter_Collect.pcb
    
    ,set,#QuantityLoop=[#QuantityLoop+1]

  , Wend


,Now that I'm done looping for the array - set the Total Unit cost here and drop it into the TAG total.
     
  
  Set, #TAGHardwareKQty=[#TAGHardwareK+#TAGHardwareKQty]
  Set, #TAGHardwareHQty=[#TAGHardwareH+#TAGHardwareHQty]
  
  Set, #TAGKCostTotal=[(#TAGHardwareK*#TempHKTotalUnitCost*NUM)+#TAGKCostTotal]
  Set, #TAGHCostTotal=[(#TAGHardwareH*#TempHKTotalUnitCost*NUM)+#TAGHCostTotal]
  Set, #TotalUnitCost=[#TAGKCostTotal+#TAGHCostTotal]
  Set, #TAGHardwareTotal=[#TAGHardwareTotal+#TotalUnitCost]
  
}
},END SKIP
